s($,"bfs","aKv",()=>A.b([A.rm("Rule 14 (Head-on): Two power-driven vessels meeting on reciprocal courses shall BOTH alter course to STARBOARD so each passes on the port side of the other.\n\nRule 15 (Crossing): When two power-driven vessels cross, the vessel having the other on her STARBOARD side shall keep out of the way and avoid crossing ahead.","COLREGs Rule 14 & 15",B.rz,B.Rp,"fc_1","What are the exact actions for Head-on (Rule 14) and Crossing (Rule 15) situations?","Remember: On head-on meeting, both alter STARBOARD. Never cross ahead of a give-way vessel."),A.rm("The 15 PPM Bilge Alarm continuously samples oily water discharge using light scattering sensors. If oil concentration exceeds 15 PPM, the monitor triggers an alarm and energizes the 3-way solenoid valve to immediately stop overboard discharge and divert water back to the bilge holding tank.","Oily Water Separator (OWS)",B.NO,B.Rr,"fc_2","Explain the working of 15 PPM Bilge Alarm Monitor and 3-Way Valve.","Key MARPOL Annex I requirement: 15 PPM max discharge with auto-stopping device."),A.rm("The Fire Tetrahedron represents the 4 essential elements needed for combustion:\n1. Fuel\n2. Heat\n3. Oxygen\n4. Uninhibited Chemical Chain Reaction (4th Component).\n\nExtinguishing agents like Halon & Dry Powder work by interrupting this chemical chain reaction.","Fire Fighting & Safety",B.N5,B.SD,"fc_3","What is the Fire Tetrahedron and its 4th component?","Traditional triangle only had Fuel, Heat, Oxygen. Tetrahedron adds the chemical reaction."),A.rm("Centrifugal Pump: Liquid churns inside casing; pressure rises to shutoff head. Can run closed briefly without instant damage.\n\nPositive Displacement Pump: Pressure rises continuously until safety relief valve opens or casing/piping ruptures. Discharge valve MUST ALWAYS BE OPEN before starting!","Auxiliary Machinery",B.Ne,B.Q7,"fc_4","What happens if you start a Centrifugal Pump vs Positive Displacement Pump with discharge valve closed?","Never start positive displacement pumps (gear, screw, piston) against a closed valve."),A.rm("An air ejector creates high vacuum (~93% / 700 mmHg) inside the FWG shell. High vacuum significantly drops the boiling point of water from 100\xb0C to approx 45\xb0C, allowing seawater to evaporate using main engine jacket cooling water (65\u201380\xb0C) as the heating source.","Fresh Water Generator",B.N2,B.Tf,"fc_5","Why does seawater boil at ~45\xb0C in a Vacuum Flash FWG?","Vacuum Flash FWG saves fuel by utilizing waste heat from engine cooling water."),A.rm("Express genuine passion for global maritime trade, international exposure, disciplined lifestyle, exposure to advanced shipboard automation, hands-on operational leadership, and clear merit-based CoC career progression to Captain/Chief Engineer.","Personal HR Interview",B.Nc,B.Ti,"fc_6","Why did you choose Merchant Navy over government or corporate shore jobs?","Show confidence, physical resilience, and commitment to long sea contracts away from home."),A.rm("SOLAS Drills: Abandon ship drill and fire drill must be conducted EVERY MONTH (or within 24h of port departure if >25% crew changed).\n\nEPIRB Frequencies: Transmits 406 MHz digital signal to Cospas-Sarsat satellites and 121.5 MHz homing signal for search and rescue aircraft.","SOLAS & LSA Regulations",B.Nn,B.SS,"fc_7","What are the SOLAS drill intervals and EPIRB distress frequencies?","EPIRB strobe light operates for at least 48 hours continuously."),A.rm("Purifier: Uses a Gravity Disc (discharge collar) selected based on oil density to establish a water seal/interface between water and oil inside the bowl.\n\nClarifier: Has NO water outlet and uses a solid Blind Disc (sealing disc) to remove fine solid impurities from oil without water separation.","Oil Purifier & Clarifier",B.Nm,B.Qc,"fc_8","How do Gravity Disc and Blind Disc differ in Purifier vs Clarifier operation?","If gravity disc size is wrong in purifier, oil will overflow from water outlet.")],A.aH("I<PX>")))
